                "retweet_count": 29,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I just spent some time in Logansport meeting with local officials who are grappling with immigration. Two takeaways:\n\u00a0\nOne: Hoosiers are kind and welcoming people, and public servants \u2013 from law enforcement to schools to the health department \u2013 are working to serve everyone.\u00a0\n\u00a0\nTwo: Immigration policy failures at the federal level take advantage of communities like Logansport, leaving them with little information and no additional resources to provide essential services.\u00a0\n\u00a0\nI\u2019m going to stay on top of this issue and do my part to ensure federal agencies are fulfilling their responsibilities.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
